In message <Y0vtb.7760$Dw6.54322@attbi_s02>, Erik Hungerbuhler wrote:
> After I ascended my Tourist last night on the Colorado server, I was 
> refreshing the Current Standings page to see where I would place and my 
> wizard who ascended a few days ago was no longer listed in the Wizard 
> class section even though he had a higher score than those currently 
> listed.  So now my Tourist is listed on the page but my Wizard is not.
> 
> My handle in the tournament is gawain.  I ascended both on the Colorado 
> server and they are right next to each other on its scoreboard.  I 
> really cannot figure out why this is happening.
> 
> Thanks
> 
> Erik

It's because each player is only eligible for one the score-based trophy.  To
quote the relevant bit from the Tournament rules on the registrations page:

#####
	We'll only be giving one prize to any given player in each set.  That means
that, though you could win Highest Score, you will not also win Highest for
your caracter class.  You could still get Most Ascensions or another additional
prize.
	No, you don't get to choose which prize you get if you would have qualified
for two.  They are ordered:
		High Score
		Highest (in each character class, alphabetically sorted)
		Second (per class)
		Third (per class)
#####

The way this works from the coreboard program's perspective is simple: as it
fills each slot n sequence, it logs that player as ineligible before
calculating the next slot.

Since they are filled alphabetically, 1st Tourist is filled before 1st Wizard
so you were moved up (from the script's perspective) to a different trophy slot.

